// `for ... nearest k to (x, y) [within r] in Index where ..` against k
// scans, each for the nearest after the one before (by how far, then by
// row): the same dots in the same order, nearest first; one, five, at
// most twelve within a distance, none, and more than there are (all).
// In a box that wraps, and of whole numbers on a lattice (many as far as
// others) over where the dots are, also from a place past the grid; and
// of three sides. The same on one core and on all.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/nearest.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.one
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/nearest.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.all
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WRAP --input-file=%t.one
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/nearest_whole.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.whole
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/nearest_whole.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.whole.all
// RUN: cmp %t.whole %t.whole.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WHOLE --input-file=%t.whole
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/nearest_3d.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.three
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/nearest_3d.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.three.all
// RUN: cmp %t.three %t.three.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=THREE --input-file=%t.three

